Spec: SpecDD Language Foundation

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Define shared SpecDD language registration and file identity.

Structure:
  ./SpecDDLanguage.kt: SpecDD language id singleton.
  ./SpecDDFileType.kt: `.sdd` file type identity and icon.
  ./SpecDDCodeStyleSettingsProvider.kt: Default editor code style for `.sdd` files.
  ./SpecDDParserDefinition.kt: Minimal PSI parser definition required by IntelliJ language services.
  ./SpecDDPsiFile.kt: PSI file wrapper for SpecDD files.
  ./parser: Shared SpecDD line classification and language facts.
  ./highlighting: Syntax highlighting concern.
  ./validation: Language validation concern.
  ./structure: Structure view concern.
  ./documentation: Hover documentation concern.
  ./completion: Section name, file path, and local symbol completion concern.
  ./references: Path and glob reference concern.

Owns:
  ./language.sdd
  ./SpecDDLanguage.sdd
  ./SpecDDFileType.sdd
  ./SpecDDCodeStyleSettingsProvider.sdd
  ./SpecDDParserDefinition.sdd
  ./SpecDDPsiFile.sdd
  ./SpecDDCodeStyleSettingsProvider.kt
  ./SpecDDLanguage.kt
  ./SpecDDFileType.kt
  ./SpecDDParserDefinition.kt
  ./SpecDDPsiFile.kt
  ./parser/*
  ./highlighting/*
  ./validation/*
  ./structure/*
  ./documentation/*
  ./completion/*
  ./references/*

Can modify:
  ./language.sdd
  ./SpecDDLanguage.sdd
  ./SpecDDFileType.sdd
  ./SpecDDCodeStyleSettingsProvider.sdd
  ./SpecDDParserDefinition.sdd
  ./SpecDDPsiFile.sdd
  ./SpecDDCodeStyleSettingsProvider.kt
  ./SpecDDLanguage.kt
  ./SpecDDFileType.kt
  ./SpecDDParserDefinition.kt
  ./SpecDDPsiFile.kt
  ./parser/*
  ./highlighting/*
  ./validation/*
  ./structure/*
  ./documentation/*
  ./completion/*
  ./references/*

Can read:
  /src/main/resources/META-INF/plugin.xml
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/*
  ./parser/*
  ./highlighting/*
  ./validation/*
  ./structure/*
  ./documentation/*
  ./completion/*
  ./references/*

Must:
  Provide default editor code style for `.sdd` files.
  Provide shared language and file-type definitions for `.sdd` files.
  Provide minimal PSI file support required by IntelliJ language services.
  Provide shared line classification when highlighting and validation need the same SpecDD syntax facts.
  Provide structure view, documentation, completion, and path reference integration for `.sdd` files.
  Keep shared language code independent from highlighting and validation behavior.
  Keep all implementation code under the `ai.specdd.idea` package namespace.
  Use `SpecDD` as the IntelliJ language id.
  Use `sdd` as the default file extension.
  Use `SpecDD` as the file type name.
  Use `SpecDD specification file` as the file type description.
  Use the packaged `META-INF/logo.svg` resource as the file type icon.
  Keep the file type as an instantiable class for IntelliJ extension point compatibility.
  Register file type, parser definition, code style provider, syntax highlighter factory, annotator, structure view factory, documentation provider, completion contributor, path reference contributor, and path warning annotator through plugin metadata.
  Use `lang.parserDefinition` for parser registration.
  Use `lang.syntaxHighlighterFactory` for syntax highlighter registration.
  Use `lang.psiStructureViewFactory` for structure view registration.
  Use `documentationProvider` for hover documentation registration.
  Use `completion.contributor` for completion contributor registration.
  Use `psi.referenceContributor` for path reference registration.
  Use `langCodeStyleSettingsProvider` for code style provider registration.
  Keep the minimum IntelliJ build at `223`.
  Keep PSI support intentionally minimal; parsing may consume the file as text while enabling language services.
  Keep default indentation, continuation indentation, and tab size at 2.
  Disable tab indentation by default.
  Expose only standard indent controls for code style settings.
  Avoid user-facing configuration UI beyond standard IntelliJ code style controls.
  Cover language id, file type metadata, parser definition, PSI file metadata, code style defaults, and plugin metadata in tests.

Must not:
  Implement syntax highlighting rules.
  Implement validation diagnostics.
  Define editor highlighting colors.
  Define validation severity or inspection messages.
  Add unrelated IDE features outside SpecDD language support.
